-- l4 batch over two DIFFERENT records of one name, `Settings`, one under
-- `§ Alpha` (limit 10) and one under `§ Beta` (limit 99), each decoded by the
-- rules. The entry for each decode carries its own heading, as the WITH entry of
-- the same record does, so the row that rests on both lists two decode entries,
-- not one for two different defaults (assumed, not ruled: the review of the
-- combined branch, 2026-10-12, following overnight card O6). The row answers 218.

§ `Alpha`

DECLARE Settings HAS
  limit IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 10

GIVEN s IS A STRING
GIVETH AN EITHER STRING Settings
parseA s MEANS JSONDECODE s

GIVETH A NUMBER
limitA MEANS CONSIDER parseA "{}"
    WHEN RIGHT st THEN st's limit
    WHEN LEFT e THEN 0

GIVETH A NUMBER
withalA MEANS (`Alpha`.Settings WITHAL)'s limit

§ `Beta`

DECLARE Settings HAS
  limit IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 99

GIVEN s IS A STRING
GIVETH AN EITHER STRING Settings
parseB s MEANS JSONDECODE s

GIVETH A NUMBER
limitB MEANS CONSIDER parseB "{}"
    WHEN RIGHT st THEN st's limit
    WHEN LEFT e THEN 0

GIVETH A NUMBER
withalB MEANS (`Beta`.Settings WITHAL)'s limit

§ `Use`

@export default both
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE both amount IS limitA PLUS limitB PLUS withalA PLUS withalB
